        "workflow": {
          "name": "archon-merge-queue",
          "description": "The merge queue: merges the pull requests the build queue finished, and stops only\nfor decisions that belong to a person. Each run claims every waiting item with\nintake's claim, up to limit. One sweep agent orders their pull requests, merges the\ndefault branch into any behind it, regenerates generated files with their owning\nscripts, and merges what policy allows, one at a time, through a gate script that\nrefuses unless the trusted review verdict says Ready at the head, CI is green there,\nno review thread is unresolved and the head contains the default branch, and merges\npinned to that head. A pull request\nwhose verdict a push made stale gets a delta review in the same run. After a batch\nthe sweep checks the default branch's CI. A clear case acts on its own; anything\nunclear pauses as one attention item whose answer is a declared choice. With mode\neval the run claims, pushes and merges nothing: it decides the replayed pull requests\nfrom the facts recorded for them and returns the decisions as its output.\n\nUse when: a trigger binding the operator installed starts it (see the SDLC pack\nREADME, \"Merge queue\"), or an operator replays recorded merge decisions in eval mode.\nNOT for: delivering or fixing a pull request (archon-build-queue, archon-ship), or\nreviewing one by hand (archon-review).\n",
